## Critical Issues

### Issue 1: npm Test Failure (Exit Code 5)

The verified test status shows:
```
npm test: exit 5 (43s)
```

This is a **test failure**, but the agent claims:
> All existing suites pass: `sw-memory-test` (22), `sw-memory-cache-test` (17), `sw-memory-index-test` (30), `sw-memory-effectiveness-test` (16)

**The discrepancy is critical:** The agent manually validated individual test suites but never ran the full `npm test` command. The exit code 5 indicates a test failure at the suite level.

### Issue 2: Missing Test File for Extracted Code

The agent extracted code into `lib/memory-query.sh` but **did not create the corresponding test file** (`sw-lib-memory-query-test.sh`). This is **Task 9**, which remains incomplete.

New code requires new tests. Moving code without tests leaves a coverage gap and violates the stated acceptance criteria:
> Create `sw-lib-memory-query-test.sh` (extraction unit tests)

This is almost certainly **why `npm test` is failing** — the test suite registration in `package.json` likely expects this file.

### Issue 3: Core Performance Optimizations Not Attempted

Tasks 4, 5, 6, 8 — the actual performance wins (index integration, LRU cap, benchmark) — haven't been started. The extraction is a prerequisite but insufficient on its own.

